    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d774">

                <pb facs="0913" n="769" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg769"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.918/43: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-31T18:00:00+08:00">July 31, 1929—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 31—12:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>657. On July 24th the American Peking editor of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Peking Leader</hi>,<anchor n="80" xml:id="d774-f1"/> published in English,
                    was notified by local authorities that Ministry of Interior had ordered
                    censorship of his paper.</p>
                <pb facs="0914" n="770" xml:id="pg770"/>
                <p>No reason for order was given, but associate editor<anchor n="81"
                        xml:id="d774-f2"/> suggests it possibly is connected with a front-page news
                    article written by him regarding the American Museum of Natural History’s forced
                    abandonment of its Central Asiatic expedition<anchor n="82" xml:id="d774-f3"/>
                    as previously reported to the Department.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Following receipt of order, the paper has sent from it proofs to censor’s
                        office, but these have promptly been stamped and returned. Editor states
                        that there have been no suggestions that all or part of any material
                        prepared for publication should be suppressed or altered and that he does
                        not for the present at least propose to enter any formal protest.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item><hi rendition="#italic">Peking Leader</hi> is incorporated under the laws
                        of Delaware, but its board of directors and stockholders are international
                        in character, including Chinese.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d774-f1" n="80" xml:id="d774-f1-content">
